Warm the neutrals and give surfaces depth (1.12.0)

Every grey sat on hue 265 — blue — with almost no chroma, which reads as
clinical rather than calm. The neutrals move to hue 55 with the same tiny
chroma: still grey, no longer cold. Primary, destructive, success and
warning keep their own hues; this is not a recolouring.

The flatness was a separate problem. In light mode the page and the cards
were both pure white, so a card was nothing but a hairline and the screen
had no depth at all. The page is warm paper now and the card is the white
one, so it lifts. Dark mode gets the same treatment through wider spacing
between background, sidebar and card.

Project cards carry a real shadow instead of shadow-xs, and lift further
on hover — feedback without adding colour.

